# Keeps the build context to what the Dockerfile actually COPYs.
#
# The Dockerfile copies six paths and nothing else:
#   css/styles.css  fonts  images  js  index.html  projects
# Everything named below sits outside that set. Nothing here may ever match
# inside those six paths, or the site ships with a missing asset and no error:
# a `COPY <dir>` whose contents are all excluded still succeeds and leaves an
# empty directory behind.
#
# Patterns match from the context root and a bare `*` does not cross `/`, so
# anything meant to match at any depth is written `**/`.
#
# Do NOT add blanket rules like `*.txt` (fonts/OFL.txt is shipped) or `*.json`
# (projects/projects.json is the gallery) or `*.js` (js/backdrop.js and
# projects/cards.js are the site).

# Version control and CI
.git
.gitignore
.github

# Agent and editor scratch
.claude
.superpowers
**/node_modules/
**/__pycache__/

# Build and deploy definitions — describe the image, never live inside it
Dockerfile
.dockerignore
compose.yml
docker-compose.yml
deploy

# Repo documentation. LICENSE and README are not served; fonts/OFL.txt is,
# and is untouched by these rules.
README.md
LICENSE

# OS droppings
**/.DS_Store
**/Thumbs.db
